  "details": "<p>\u00a0The area of the Meta Sudans has been explored by extensive archaeological excavation under Clementina Panella.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A large fountain located southwest of the Flavian Amphitheater and completed under Domitian (ca. A.D. 96). Four of Rome's Augustan regions converged at this point (I, III, IV, X); it is possible that Regio II also intersected the other four regiones at this place.",
